    "updated_at": "2022-04-11T15:41:56Z",
    "body": "thanks @davidkna . following your advice on for git status I was able to substantially drop the git time. \r\n\r\nhere are the settings I used for python\r\n```toml\r\n[python]\r\npyenv_version_name = true\r\npython_binary = [\"python\"]\r\nformat = 'via [${symbol}${version}]($style)'\r\n```\r\nwhich reduced the time on python by almost half\r\n```sh\r\nHere are the timings of modules in your prompt (>=1ms or output):\r\n python      -  83ms  -   \"via 🐍 myenv\"\r\n git_status  -  29ms  -   \"[$!?] \"\r\n directory   -  14ms  -   \"my_project \"\r\n package     -  12ms  -   \"\"\r\n battery     -   2ms  -   \"\"\r\n pulumi      -   2ms  -   \"\"\r\n git_commit  -   1ms  -   \"\"\r\n git_branch  -  <1ms  -   \"on  my_branch \"\r\n line_break  -  <1ms  -   \"\\n\"\r\n character   -  <1ms  -   \"➜ \"\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
